ject} into the plan — an execution step that confirms the implementation works via the fastest local run or manual probe against the real target, before it is committed to the slow delivery loop.\",\n      \"applies_when\": [\"T15\"],\n  }\n\nSupersedes the earlier draft template ('Prove {subject} with the fastest out-of-loop experiment ... before committing it to the slow delivery loop'), which read as a planning-time activity and overlapped spike.","timestamp":1784919283159287001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Operator APPROVED the refined move 15 verbatim. Ticket promoted from proposal to implementation: title/description finalized with the approved template as acceptance criteria. No longer pending.","timestamp":1784919374062375001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan-review remediation and collision resolution: the deterministic blockers were the nonstandard acceptance heading and missing Testing section; both are fixed with atomized observable criteria and real commands. Repository inspection also proved that id 15 is now occupied by the landed `sample, not the population` move from closed ticket amoral-natatorial-dog. The approved out-of-loop-proof content is therefore allocated the next free id, 16, while preserving move 15. Added the registry consumers required by current main: the mirrored gate-doc table, the plan-writing guide index, exact/scoped/rendering tests, and guide tests. A depends_on link to the closed predecessor was attempted for provenance but correctly rejected because rebar does not add blocking links to closed targets; the predecessor is cited directly in this plan and comment instead.","timestamp":1786565188334932001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Applied the signed review P6 advisory: split the two compound acceptance outcomes into independently verifiable name, template, placeholder, selection, deterministic rendering, move-15 preservation, and author-guide outcomes. No implementation scope changed. Refreshing plan review before claim.","timestamp":1786565733918606001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"RED oracle evidence: collected and executed 7 intended cases; all 7 failed for the missing move-16 behavior (registry/load KeyError, Pass-4 selection dropped the unknown move, and real `rebar explain plan` output lacked the author guidance). Contract card: authority is this ticket’s approved verbatim template and ACs; production paths are built-in registry -> strict validator/applicability -> Pass-4 deterministic renderer plus packaged guide -> real CLI; exact postconditions are id/name/template/single placeholder/T15-only trigger, deterministic rendered coaching, negative non-T15 exclusion, and execution-vs-planning guidance; existing move-15 lock tests are the collateral invariant; gate is the focused plan-review/review-kernel/guide suite and project preflight. No state, recovery, or contention mechanism applies.","timestamp":1786573282285465001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Held-out validation: implementer completed in one attempt and saw only the exact registry/validator happy path. After restoring the off-limits oracle, 6/7 initially passed; the sole failure was my whitespace/contiguity assumption in the CLI prose test, not missing behavior. Under revert-first discipline I removed the guide bullet, corrected the test to assert the separate semantic consequences, reconfirmed RED because the move guidance was absent, restored the unchanged guide implementation, and reached 7/7 GREEN. Defect-seeded mutation changed applies_when from T15 to T14; both the held-out applicability test and real Pass-4 selection test went RED, then the production line was restored.","timestamp":1786573485441765001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Preflight complete. Full held-out focused suite: 190 passed. Criteria routing parity: 44 criteria in sync. make lint passed (including complexity baseline and workflow checks). make typecheck passed (513 files). git diff --check passed; coach_moves.py is 220 LOC under the 800 LOC cap. Full canonical make test: 12,451 passed, 62 skipped, 269 deselected, 38 warnings in 43m29s. No failures.","timestamp":1786576184234096001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Final-base validation: origin/main advanced by three unrelated, non-overlapping changes during the first full run. Commit rebased cleanly onto 3c1972e9c0. Post-rebase focused suite 190 passed; lint/typecheck/diff/trailer checks passed. Exact final rebased commit full make test: 12,482 passed, 54 skipped, 269 deselected, 38 warnings in 44m48s.","timestamp":1786578991162210001}],"created_at":1784918872615525001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"185c7c6d-d851-4832-8190-4122418161e5","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"ea28-020e-8215-4eb9"},{"link_uuid":"3a64220c-aecc-4920-aca0-c438f9c2740f","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"5ffc-0a45-ed8f-43fe"}],"description":"APPROVED (operator sign-off recorded 2026-07-24). Add a new Pass-4 coach move for T15 findings. Existing moves 1 (spike), 4 (riskiest-assumption test), and 7 (thin vertical slice) are adjacent but none captures the T15 remedy. The move is deliberately distinct from move 1: spike is a PLANNING-TIME experiment before plan approval that proves a mechanism or syntax and yields a decision; out-of-loop proof is an EXECUTION-TIME step the plan itself includes to prove the actual implementation works before it enters the slow delivery loop.\n\nMove id 15 was available when this story was approved, but it has since landed as `sample, not the population` under closed ticket `amoral-natatorial-dog`. Preserve that shipped move unchanged and allocate the next free built-in id, 16, to this approved move.\n\n## Work\n- Add key `16` to `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/coach_moves.py` `MOVE_REGISTRY` with name `out-of-loop proof`, the approved template below verbatim, and `applies_when: [\"T15\"]`:\n\n  `Build an out-of-loop proof of {subject} into the plan — an execution step that confirms the implementation works via the fastest local run or manual probe against the real target, before it is committed to the slow delivery loop.`\n- Preserve move 15 and every other existing registry entry unchanged.\n- Add the matching move-16 row to the mirrored coaching table in `docs/plan-review-gate.md`.\n- Add `out-of-loop proof` to the remaining registered moves in `src/rebar/_guides/writing-a-passing-plan.md`, describing it as an execution step before the slow delivery loop rather than a planning-time spike.\n- Extend `tests/unit/test_plan_review.py` with exact registry, scoped-applicability, deterministic-rendering, and negative-trigger contracts for move 16.\n- Extend `tests/unit/test_guides.py` with the observable author-guide one-line contract.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `MOVE_REGISTRY[\"16\"]` has name `out-of-loop proof`.\n- [ ] `MOVE_REGISTRY[\"16\"]` contains the approved template verbatim.\n- [ ] The move-16 template contains exactly one `{subject}` placeholder.\n- [ ] `MOVE_REGISTRY[\"16\"]` declares exactly `[\"T15\"]` in `applies_when`.\n- [ ] `validate_move_registry` accepts the complete built-in registry with move 16.\n- [ ] A surviving T15 finding can select move 16.\n- [ ] Move 16 renders the approved template deterministically with the bounded subject substituted.\n- [ ] Move 16 is not offered when T15 is absent from the active finding criteria.\n- [ ] Move 15 remains named `sample, not the population`.\n- [ ] Move 15 retains its existing template.\n- [ ] Move 15 retains its existing `[\"G1G2\", \"E4\", \"G6\", \"A1\"]` trigger set.\n- [ ] The move table in `docs/plan-review-gate.md` mirrors move 16 exactly.\n- [ ] The author guide names `out-of-loop proof`.\n- [ ] The author guide distinguishes move 16 as an execution-time step from the planning-time `spike` move.\n- [ ] The focused plan-review and review-kernel suites pass with the new scoped move.\n\n## Testing\n- Run `.venv/bin/pytest tests/unit/test_plan_review.py tests/unit/test_review_kernel.py tests/unit/test_guides.py -q`.\n- Run `.venv/bin/python -m rebar.llm.plan_review.registry validate-routing`.\n- Run `make lint` and `make typecheck`.\n- Inspect the registry diff to confirm it adds move 16 without modifying move 15 or another existing move.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/coach_moves.py","reason":"add approved T15 out-of-loop-proof move as next free built-in id 16"},{"path":"docs/plan-review-gate.md","reason":"mirror move 16 in the coaching move table"},{"path":"src/rebar/_guides/writing-a-passing-plan.md","reason":"document the new registered move for plan authors"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_plan_review.py","reason":"exact template, trigger, applicability, rendering, and docs-table contracts"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_guides.py","reason":"author-guide contract for the out-of-loop-proof move"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["depends_on","ea28-020e-8215-4eb9"],["parent","8fc2-0306-a9a0-4864"],["relates_to","5ffc-0a45-ed8f-43fe"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"8fc2-0306-a9a0-4864","parent_status_uuid":"fb0da421-7835-4b60-b34e-ca56e10cfc4f","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"754c-f6bd-0326-4ee8","ticket_type":"story","title":"Add coach move 16 'out-of-loop proof' (